# Single scratch tree — all machine-local working state, in three lifecycle
# tiers. Only this .gitignore and the per-tier .gitkeep files are tracked, so
# the tree exists on fresh clones; everything else is local, never committed.
#
#   drafts/   durable agent-draft DATA — expensive in-progress pipeline
#             artifacts that must survive between sessions: attribution
#             sibling drafts at drafts/attribution-{slug}/, OCR page reads +
#             confirm log at drafts/ocr-{stem}/. A multi-hour producer run is
#             the costliest artifact the sibling pipelines emit, and /tmp
#             cleanup has destroyed drafts before (/tmp is tmpfs — erased on
#             every reboot — plus a 10-day age purge). Owners of the output
#             paths: the prepare-transcript-sibling / prepare-ocr-sibling
#             SKILL.md files and the attribution-producer / ocr-page-producer
#             contracts.
#   queries/  throwaway exploratory query SCRIPTS — the contributor landing
#             zone (see scripts/README.md). When a query class repeats across
#             sessions, graduate it to scripts/tools/ as a proper subcommand.
#   cache/    regenerable-but-EXPENSIVE derived state (ocr-consensus engine
#             reads, keyed by pdf+dpi+engine versions). Prune-safe anytime —
#             the owning tool recomputes on a miss — but costly enough that
#             /tmp cleanup must not silently evict it.
#
# The boundary is regeneration cost, not uniformity: cheap regenerable scratch
# (extract-source.py plaintext, worker fragments, extracted frames, renders)
# stays in /tmp.
#
# Lifecycle — durable, not immortal: a top-level entry in drafts/ or queries/
# lives while it is referenced by path from meta/BACKLOG.md / meta/roadmap.md
# (parked cross-session work named by the open item that owns it) or modified
# within the grace window; the scratch-hygiene pre-commit gate
# (scripts/tests/scratch-hygiene.sh) blocks the commit on anything else, and
# on any top-level entry that is not one of the three tiers. cache/ is exempt
# from referenced-or-fresh (a content-addressed cache is not parked work); the
# gate reports its size when it grows large. Closing a work item includes
# sweeping its scratch — deletion stays human (age-based auto-deletion is the
# /tmp failure this tree exists to prevent).
*
!.gitignore
!drafts/
drafts/*
!drafts/.gitkeep
!queries/
queries/*
!queries/.gitkeep
!cache/
cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep
